abstract: >-
  Source code and container of the algorithm submitted by team STRATIF-AI-BRE
  (published on Grand Challenge as "BRE SEG") to the ISLES'26 challenge, held at
  the SWITCH+ workshop of MICCAI 2026 (27 September 2026). It segments ischaemic
  stroke lesions on skull-stripped T1-weighted brain MRI at acute, sub-acute and
  chronic stages. The model is a 3D nnU-Net v2 with a ResEnc-L residual encoder,
  trained on a center-disjoint split solved by mixed-integer linear programming
  and on a percentile-clipped z-score normalisation computed inside the brain
  mask; the prediction is an ensemble of three fold models with mirroring
  test-time augmentation. Research software, not a medical device. Developed
  within the STRATIF-AI project, funded by the European Union under Horizon
  Europe (grant agreement No 101080875).
keywords:
